``` CL-03 | Search Factor / Replication Factor Not Met: Which Buckets, Which Peers
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: The cluster manager reports Search Factor or Replication Factor
    Not Met; identify the affected indexes and the peers that originated the
    under-replicated buckets.
    Run on: CM.
    Query: Cluster-wide flags (CM)
    If this returns nothing, run probes/CL-03-probe-rest1.spl,
    probes/CL-03-probe-rest2.spl, probes/CL-03-probe-rest3.spl to confirm the
    data it reads exists here.
```
| rest splunk_server=local /services/cluster/master/health
| table replication_factor search_factor all_peers_are_up all_data_is_searchable
